plays.verse:
We are such things as dreams of fire and foam,
But lo, our forms do match the echo's tone;
Each phrase weaves like threads upon a thread.

drafts.tidy:
We are such things as dreams of fire and foam,
But lo, our forms do match the echo's tone;
Each phrase weaves like threads upon a thread.

O brave new world, that has such people in it!
I stand upon the edge where dawn ascends,
My voice a feather on the wind's soft sighs;

plays.verse:
Boldly stands I, brave and clear,
The night's cold breath my spirit veers near;
Yet now I cast my gaze to sky.

drafts.tidy:
Boldly stands I, brave and clear,
The night's cold breath my spirit veers near;
Yet now I cast my gaze to sky.

Fear not this tongue sharpened by fire,
Let me strike back, my blade already sired;
Both foes shall meet at breath’s unsteady cry—

To be, I wake within this mortal frame,
A mask of sorrow masks my mad desire deep;
Would death's hollow night in moonlit shade keep?
